  "term": "lead",
  "says": "A cutting lead: one voice at a time, a bright harmonic source (saw, or saw against a square) through a low-pass open enough that the energy sits in the upper mids where a melody is heard over a mix, a short attack so it hits the beat, a touch of drive for edge, narrow in stereo (a lead in the middle, not wide), often with a little portamento between notes. The judge's target of the same name. Signature: an attack under 50 ms, harmonic, a centroid in the upper mids, more energy above 2.5 kHz than a bass or a pad, narrow.",
